{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1472278-awakened-anima-homebrew-sorcerous-initiation-many-many-evocations","id":1472278,"title":"Awakened Anima (Homebrew Sorcerous Initiation + Many, Many Evocations)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-11T16:07:51-08:00","id":1472278,"title":"Awakened Anima (Homebrew Sorcerous Initiation + Many, Many Evocations)","content":"So I had this basic idea back in 2ed days, but 3ed Sorcerous Initiations helped me flesh it out. The Initiation itself is one thing, an attached Merit grants sorcerer's a weapon, and Exalted Sorcerers can unlock the proposed Evocations from it based on their anima. <br /> <br /> The basic premise of the evocations is that each caste has three sets of Evocations, each based on one of their three anima abilities (Solars have three per set at Ess 1, 2 &amp; 3, Dragonbloods have two since they start at Essence 2 by default). The Ess 4 Evocation is a way of combining these into a power that is relevant to that caste, and the E5 charm is generic, but reflects each Caste's own uniqueness. But these are all just ideas and can be separated from the actual Initiation itself, which I like just fine on its own.<br /> <br /> <b>Note: </b>I am not good especially at Exalted balancing so some of this will be useless and/or broken. But I wanted to get it down in writing. <br /> <br /> - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted 3rd Edition, p24</i></b></div> <div align=\"center\"><i><b>Anima:</b> All living things are surrounded by a colorless, invisible aura called anima. When one of the Exalted uses Essence, the power often spills into her anima, making it visible.<br /> As a result, an Exalt who expends a great deal of power is usually engulfed by a display of anima that can range from a soft glow to a pillar of heatless \ufb02ame bright enough to see for miles.</i></div> <br /> <br /> <b>Awakened Anima (Sorcerous Initiation)</b><br /> <br /> Every being in Creation, from the lowest slave to the highest Queen is encircled by a permanent aura emanating from their soul. Unseen and unfelt, most will never even know it exists. But in the high first age, powerful mystics carved arcane sigils and tattooed essence-enhancing mudras into their animas, shaping the essence that passes through it and performing miracles. These secrets have survived, passed down from teacher to student across the ages, across both Creation and Heaven.<br /> <br /> Any sorcerer who use these Shaping rituals causes their anima to glow in the same way as an Exalt using peripheral essence. For any Sorcerer with one of these Shaping Rituals, taking a single Shaping (or Distort/Counterspell) action that accrues 5+ successes raises her anima banner one level; from Dim to Glowing to Burning to Bonfire. <br /> <br /> <u>A note on non-Exalted Sorcerers:</u> <br /> Non-Exalted humans who use these rituals will, by default, raise a silent banner of pale white light. The animas of some Spirits, Godbloods and stranger beings might display other colours and manifestations, though none will have a caste mark, nor an iconic display.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shaping Rituals</b><br /> <br /> <u>Essence Gathering Approach</u><br /> A Sorcerer with an Essence pool may spend a scene in meditation to commit ten motes to her anima. Once she begins shaping a spell, she may draw on the power she\u2019s invested, contributing up to (Essence + 2) sorcerous motes towards the spell until the full commitment of motes has been converted, or the spell is cast (or countered). Committed motes are converted to sorcerous motes on a one-to-one basis normally, but are converted into two sorcerous motes when casting the sorcerer\u2019s control spell <br /> <br /> <u>Tearing the Tapestry</u><br /> Her anima shining like a divine mirror, the Sorcerer reverses the spells of her enemies. When she makes a Counterspell or Distortion attempt she adds 1 (Glowing), 2 (Burning) or 3 (Bonfire) successes to the attempt based on her current anima level. Once a scene per spell, unless she knows the spell she is opposing.<br /> <br /> <u>Aura of Magic</u><br /> Her anima is the manifestation of the Sorcerer\u2019s soul. This energy vibrates sympathetically when she embraces life and rejects death. If the Sorcerer has rolled Join Battle but not caused health or initiative damage to a living being, she adds (Essence) dice to her Shape Sorcery actions. The requirement of this ritual includes Spirits and animals, but not the Dead (who live no longer) nor Fae (which were never truly alive).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Other Benefits</b><br /> <br /> <b>Shinmaic Nimbus</b> (Merit \u25cf - \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): The Sorcerer arranges the symbols and glyphs in her anima just so, revealing their new pattern for all to see as essence spills into it. Whilst her anima is visible, the Sorcerer gains mutation dots equal to her dots in this merit. When her anima increases a level she decides whether to manifest all or none of these mutations, but cannot selectively choose between mutations. These transformations are part of her anima banner and appear in it\u2019s colour and style. Once per story she may undertake occult research (Appearance+Occult, dif 3) and change the mutations that she manifests. <br /> <br /> <b>Weaving of Wonders </b>(Merit \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): The arcane sigils scribed into the Sorcerer\u2019s anima function as sorcerous infrastructure, granting +1 Means. Furthermore, by using her instinctive familiarity with her anima as a tool to shape the essence of Creation, she is able to perform sorcerous workings more quickly than usual - though risking her working\u2019s collapse in her expedience:<br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Reduce Terminus by 1 - each interval takes 1 day - increase base difficulty by 1</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Reduce Terminus by 2 - each interval takes 12 hours - increase base difficulty by 2</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Reduce Terminus by 3 - each interval takes 1 hour - increase base difficulty by 2</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Reduce Terminus by 4 - each interval takes 30 minutes - increase base difficulty by 2</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Reduce Terminus by 5 - each interval takes 1 minute - increase base difficulty by 3</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Reduce Terminus by 6 - each interval takes 30 seconds - increase base difficulty by 3</div> <br /> <b>Lance of the Sorcerer-Queen </b>(Merit \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf): Channelling her anima outward, the Sorcerer unleashes a flash of concentrated magic that strikes a target with raw force. Rolling (Perception+Occult), this is treated as a mundane archery weapon with the Bashing, Mounted, One-Handed and Special tags. It cannot be disarmed by any means and does not add the user\u2019s Strength to Withering damage. Additionally;<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">at Dim or Glowing level, her anima has Light weapon traits and the Archery (Short) tag</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">at Burning level, her anima has Medium weapon traits and the Archery (Medium) tag</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">at Bonfire level, her anima has Heavy weapon traits and the Archery (Long) tag</div> <br /> A Sorcerer with an essence pool may commit 5 motes to her anima to attune to it and treat it as an artifact archery weapon instead, using the stats of the appropriate weight category. She may also awaken Evocations in her anima - example evocation trees are below.<br /> <br /> - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - <br /> <br /> <b>Lance of the Sorcerer-Queen</b><br /> <i>Attunement</i>: 5m<br /> <i>Type: </i>Light / Medium / Heavy<br /> <i>Tags:</i> Archery (Short / Medium / Long), Bashing, Mounted, Special<br /> <i>Hearthstone Slots:</i> 0<br /> <i>Era:</i> Various (first recorded during the Warmage Crusades)<br /> Evocations of Lance of the Sorcerer-Queen: The Lance\u2019s basic evocations enhance its Sorcerer\u2019s attacks and let her mould her anima. The animas of the Chosen however are shaped by their caste or aspect. They may also awaken evocations which build on their inherent anima powers, eventually blending them to transform the Exalted Sorcerer into a living representation of their innate glory. Upon attunement, the Sorcerer unlocks any Essence 1 evocation for which she qualifies without cost.<br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <b>Basic Evocations - Any Sorcerer with an Essence Pool</b></div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Arcane Flash</b><br /> Cost: 3m+; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Withering-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> The wise know when flight is preferable to fight. The Sorcerer pays three motes to make a withering attack dazzlingly bright; a target damaged by the attack is blinded for 1 round per 3 motes spent. The Sorcerer does not gain the target's lost initiative but still gains 1i for landing a successful withering attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Wicked Thrust Technique</b><br /> Cost: 3m or 6m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> For 3 motes, the Sorcerer may grant a single decisive attack with her Lance the Lethal and Smashing tags. Alternatively, for 6 motes, she creates a burst of essence which inflicts bashing damage against her target and all those within short range of him, dividing her initiative amongst them equally. She is reset to base initiative as long as at least one target suffers damage. Battlegroups reduce their Defence by 1 when struck by the second version. <br /> <br /> <b>Ephemeral Shield Stance</b><br /> Cost: 1m+, 1WP; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> Pouring essence into her anima, the Sorcerer momentarily gives it substance. She gains magical Soak on a 1:1 basis for each mote spent against one withering attack, up to (Essence) motes. Alternatively, she gains 1 Hardness for every two motes spent against one Decisive attack, same maximum. Soak stacks with natural / armour soak but not other magic. Hardness does not stack.<br /> <br /> <b>Cloak of Pearls and Diamonds</b><br /> Cost: 3m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Mute, Stackable<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Ephemeral Shield Stance</i><br /> The Sorcerer commits the motes and creates a pocket of tangible essence within her anima. For as long as the motes remain committed, this pocket functions as a hearthstone socket. The Sorcerer may create up to (Essence) such sockets. Socketed hearthstones orbit closely around the sorcerer; a difficulty 4 Unsocket Gambit can shatter a pocket, ending its commitment and causing the hearthstone to fall undamaged to the ground.<br /> <br /> <b>Sword of Creation Emulation</b><br /> Cost: 3a, 1WP; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Aggravated, Decisive-Only, <br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Arcane Flash, Wicked Thrust Technique</i><br /> This Evocation treats the Sorcerer\u2019s lance as cold iron for the scene, allowing her to shred the unearthly bodies of the Wyld-born with ease. All of her lance attacks deal aggravated damage to Fae for the scene. </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T16:09:40-08:00","id":1472279,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <b>Solar Evocations </b>- <i>The Solar\u2019s Lance is treated as an orichalcum weapon for any relevant purposes</i></div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Solar Exalted - Dawn Caste</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>At bonfire/iconic anima display, the Dawn adds half her Essence score (round up) to her base Initiative upon resetting to base after a successful decisive attack.</i></div> <br /> <b>Golden Within As Without</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only, (Dawn Caste-only)<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> Using this Evocation when she resets to base initiative, the Dawn may add (Essence/2, round up) to her base initiative regardless of her anima level. She adds a further +1 when at bonfire level.<br /> <br /> <b>Flawless Warrior\u2019s Stance</b><br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Golden Within As Without</i><br /> The Dawn stands unphased in the direst of circumstances. Opponents no longer gain an automatic 1i for landing a successful attack against her.<br /> <br /> <b>Escalating Force Method</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only, Perilous<br /> Duration: One Scene or until ended<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Flawless Warrior\u2019s Stance</i><br /> The Dawn activates this charm when rolling Join Battle or resetting to base initiative. She adds an additional +1 to her base initiative each time she subsequently resets to it following a successful decisive attack. These increases stack for the rest of the scene, but if a reset was forced upon her by an opponent or by entering Initiative Crash, the charm ends and her base initiative returns to normal.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <i>For 10 motes, all of the Dawn\u2019s combat and movement Charms with outstanding reset conditions are automatically reset. This effect can only be used once per day, becoming available again at sunrise.</i></div> <br /> <b>Sharing the Sun </b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Mute, (Dawn Caste-only)<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> When the Dawn resets her combat and movement charms with her anima, she may share this benefit with (Essence/2) allies within:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Short range if her anima is at Dim or Glowing level; <br /> Medium range if it is at Burning level; or<br /> Long range if it is at Bonfire level.</div> <br /> <b>Daybreak Waking Technique</b><br /> Cost: 6i; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Sharing the Sun</i><br /> When the Dawn resets her combat and movement charms with her anima, she is treated as having had a full night\u2019s rest. Her fatigue and onslaught penalties drops to zero and she regains a point of temporary willpower, up to her maximum. <br /> <br /> <b>First Light Benediction</b><br /> Cost: 4m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites:<i> Daybreak Waking Technique</i><br /> As shadows recede, the Dawn is reborn. When she resets her combat and movement charms with her anima, she also heals up to (Essence) damaged bashing or lethal health levels and adds up to (Essence+Willpower) motes to her mote pools (peripheral first). This benefit is not shared when using Sharing The Sun.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <i>The Dawn Caste inspires terror in her foes. She adds half her Essence score (round up) in dice to all intimidating social influence. She may also intimidate targets which do not feel fear, such as automatons, golems, and certain undead.</i></div> <br /> <b>Bronze Tiger\u2019s Roar</b><br /> Cost: 6m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Psyche, (Dawn Caste-only)<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> A foe\u2019s soul quivers under the Dawn\u2019s gaze. When the Solar makes a Threaten action the target is treated as having a Minor Tie of Submissive Terror towards her. He must enter a decision point and pay the higher of (Solar\u2019s Essence or 2) Willpower to resist this influence.<br /> <br /> <b>Terrifying Brilliance Prana</b><br /> Cost: 3m, 3i; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites:<i> Bronze Tiger\u2019s Roar</i><br /> So terrifying is the Dawn that opposing forces lose their composure entirely. A battlegroup successfully struck by her reduces their Drill score by one level - from Elite, to Average to Poor for the scene. Units which already have Poor drill must immediately make a Rout check. <br /> <br /> <b>All-Encompassing Commander Stance</b><br /> Cost: 9m; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Terrifying Brilliance Prana</i><br /> The Dawn is leadership personified. When an opposing battlegroup fails a Rout check, the Solar makes a special Command roll against the Battlegroup\u2019s previous Resolve. On a success, she barks orders to the fleeing force and they are too intimidated to refuse her. They reform at their previous size-1, with Poor Drill and obey the Solar for the remainder of the scene, or until she fails to make a successful Command roll for them.<br /> <br /> <b>Heaven\u2019s Unending Blade Practice</b><br /> Cost: 1WP; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Until ended<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>All-Encompassing Commander Stance, Escalating Force Method, First Light Benediction</i><br /> Nothing stops a Dawn in pursuit of victory. When she makes a successful decisive attack, this evocation allows her to move up to one range band and make a decisive attack against another non-trivial target using the same initiative roll. This repeats until there are no further valid targets in range or she can move no further, at which point she resets to base initiative. She cannot attack the same target more than once with this effect, but battlegroups may be targeted up to (Size) times.<br /> <br /> <b>Avatar of the Ascending Sun</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Dual, Perilous, Uniform<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Heaven\u2019s Unending Blade Practice</i><br /> The Dawn is the embodiment of the Sun's facet her caste represents, her Anima rising to iconic level and unable to subside or be shed until the end of the scene. Whilst this Evocation is active, she awakens the power from the list below that matches her Supernal ability and (Essence-3) others:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Archery: </b>The Dawn can make archery attacks at extreme range (up to (Essence) range bands). She must still aim to do so beyond Short range.<br /> <b>Awareness: </b>The Dawn may substitute any sense for another without penalty. She can hear colours and taste conversations.<br /> <b>Brawl: </b>The Dawn\u2019s unarmed attacks gain the balanced, chopping, lethal, piercing, smashing and two-handed tags. She may parry lethal damage without other magic. <br /> <b>Dodge:</b> The Dawn may apply her Dodge defence against an undodgeable attack for 1WP.<br /> <b>Martial Arts: </b>When the Dawn uses a form charm, she may reflexively activate a second form charm she knows and benefit from both simultaneously.<br /> <b>Melee: </b>The Dawn may apply her Parry defence against an unblockable attack for 1WP.<br /> <b>Resistance:</b> The Dawn converts half of Aggravated damage to Lethal, and all other Lethal damage to Bashing. Damage still rolls over.<br /> <b>Thrown:</b> The Dawn can make thrown attacks at extreme range (up to (Essence) range bands). She must still aim to do so beyond Short range.<br /> <b>War:</b> Battlegroups the Dawn commands possess Might +1 (max 2).</div> <br /> Additionally, she adds (Essence/2, round down) non-charm dice to any action using her Supernal ability.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Solar Exalted - Zenith Caste</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>For one mote, the Zenith\u2019s anima leaps from her hand to a corpse she\u2019s touching, igniting it in Solar flame. This power incinerates the corpse and ensures the soul of the deceased will not return as a hungry ghost. In addition, the Zenith may perceive the strongest Intimacies of the deceased and may choose to accept them. When she is ready, she may pay one mote, touching a target of those Intimacies to pass on feelings of peace, love, and assurance, shedding them in the process. She may also transfer them to an object, allowing it to convey comfort or a sense of duty to the subject. Conversely, she may touch someone who caused the deceased to suffer, paying one mote and rolling ([A social Attribute] + Presence) with three automatic non-Charm successes against their Resolve to transfer pain suffered by the deceased back on the one who caused it. The Storyteller is free to dictate the length and weight of such attrition.</i></div> <br /> <b>Dutiful Shepherd\u2019s Grace</b><br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: - (Zenith Caste-only)<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> When the Zenith passes on positive feelings to someone or an object after accepting someone\u2019s intimacies, she regains a point of temporary Willpower. When she successfully passes on negative feelings with this anima power, she instead heals (Essence) bashing or lethal health levels. <br /> <br /> <b>Solar Oneiromancy Method</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Stackable<br /> Duration: One night's sleep<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Dutiful Shepherd\u2019s Grace</i><br /> In sleep, the Zenith shares her dreams with those whose intimacies she carries in her anima. She may learn things they knew in life related to the intimacies she carries, mechanically represented by asking the ST a question on the relevant topic. She may ask as many questions during a night as she wishes and has motes to pay to activate this Evocation. However, each intimacy may only be questioned once, and if all intimacies are questioned that person\u2019s intimacies are released, meaning they can never be passed on.<br /> <br /> <b>Strength of Lethe Invocation</b><br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Permanent (Instant)<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Solar Oneiromancy Method</i><br /> The emotions the Zenith carries instinctively work to protect her, to ensure she may continue and pass them on. Once per session, when the Zenith would gain Limit by opposing a Major or Defining intimacy, she may instead substitute an appropriate Major or Defining intimacy from someone whose intimacies she has accepted, to negate the Limit roll. The Zenith does not know about the Great Curse, but deep down she feels a swell of gratitude and gains the Minor Principle \u201cI must pass on that person\u2019s feelings\u201d which never degrades until she successfully does so.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <i>For 10 motes, one Willpower, the Zenith channels her Essence into an aura of divine retribution, surging around an attack. This power supplements a successful decisive attack against a creature of darkness, preventing the Solar\u2019s Initiative from returning to its base value after the attack. When the Zenith\u2019s anima is at bonfire, reduce the cost of this power by five motes and ignore the Willpower. This power may only be used once per day, resetting when the sun is at its zenith.</i></div> <br /> <b>Purge the Unclean Prana</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1a; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only, Perilous, (Zenith Caste-only)<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> This Evocation allows the Zenith to make further decisive attacks against nn-trivial Creatures of Darkness without returning to base initiative. The Zenith may not attack a target already affected by this anima power in the scene, but battlegroups composed mostly of Creatures of Darkness may be targeted up to (Size) times.<br /> <br /> <b>Bulwark Against Sin Stance</b><br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Purge the Unclean Prana</i><br /> When her anima is at bonfire level, Creatures of Darkness within close range of the Zenith are subject to the rules of Anima Flux. She rolls one die of withering damage at the start of each turn, or one die of decisive lethal damage to crashed and trivial opponents.<br /> <br /> <b>Karma Manifesting Method</b><br /> Cost: 6i, 1WP; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Aggravated, Decisive-only<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Bulwark Against Sin Stance</i><br /> Whilst this Evocation is active, the Zenith\u2019s Lance attacks deal aggravated damage to Creatures of Darkness with Essence equal to or less than hers. Those with higher Essence scores instead suffer lethal damage.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <i>For seven motes, the Zenith may order a dematerialized spirit to manifest using a (Charisma + Presence) persuade action with (Essence) automatic successes. All spirits inherently recognize the Unconquered Sun\u2019s authority in the priest-kings and are compelled as if by a Defining Intimacy, but may still have Defining Ties or Principles which counter this advantage. If successful, the Zenith\u2019s very command draws the spirit into the material world, so that it does not need to pay the cost to materialize.</i></div> <br /> <b>Ephemera Shedding Shout</b><br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: - (Zenith Caste-only)<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> This Evocation allows the Zenith to exercise their authority in both directions. She may now pay the motes and roll to command a spirit to dematerialise as well as ordering them to appear.<br /> <br /> <b>Servant of the Sun Prana</b><br /> Cost: 3m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: (Essence) rounds<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Ephemera Shedding Shout</i><br /> When the Zenith successfully commands a spirit to materialise, she may use this evocation to have it retain the Defining Intimacy compelling it to obey her for (Essence) rounds. During this time, the Zenith may again leverage her authority manifested in this Intimacy to use social influence on the spirit.<br /> <br /> <b>Mudra of Banishment</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Servant of the Sun Prana</i><br /> Drawing the sigil of The Master Key in her anima, the Zenith locks a spirit out of Creation. Using this evocation against a materialised spirit she rolls (Charisma+Performance) against the spirit\u2019s Resolve. If successful, the spirit is banished to its sanctum; if it lacks one it is sent to the most appropriate other realm (Gods to Yu Shan, Demons to Malfeas, Ghosts to the Underworld, Elementals to the sanctum of the local Censor.)<br /> <br /> <b>Bellow of the Golden Bull</b><br /> Cost: 6i, 1a; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Karma Manifesting Technique, Mudra of Banishment, Strength of Lethe Invocation </i><br /> Raising her arms high, the Zenith calls out a prayer to Heaven and brings down judgement upon the wicked. Her anima swirls outward, taking the form of a battlegroup of golden warriors. This battlegroup uses the stats of Elite troops with Elite Drill, Might 1 and is (Essence) size. The battlegroup never routs and automatically succeeds such checks. If facing primarily Creatures of Darkness they have Might 2. If opposing the target of a carried Defining negative intimacy, the battlegroup gains +1 Size.<br /> <br /> <b>Avatar of the Resplendent Sun</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Psyche, Uniform<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Bellow of the Golden Bull</i><br /> The Zenith is the embodiment of the Sun's facet her caste represents, her Anima rising to iconic level and unable to subside or be shed until the end of the scene. Whilst this Evocation is active, she awakens the power from the list below that matches her Supernal ability and (Essence-3) others:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Athletics: </b>The Zenith adds her (Essence) to her Strength when determining what Feats of Strength and Destruction she can undertake.<br /> <b>Integrity: </b>The Zenith is immune to Psyche keyword charms.<br /> <b>Performance: </b>Those within Long range of the Zenith are inspired by her perfect elegance, gaining (Zenith\u2019s Essence/2) additional motes at the end of the round.<br /> <b>Lore:</b> The Zenith may introduce a single fact that is not internally consistent, but remains a fact until the end of the scene. Once per story.<br /> <b>Presence: </b>Any opponent within Long range of the Zenith must move a range band towards her every round unless they roll (Willpower), difficulty (Zenith\u2019s Essence).<br /> <b>Resistance: </b>The Zenith converts half of Aggravated damage to Lethal, and all other Lethal damage to Bashing. Damage still rolls over.<br /> <b>Survival: </b>The Zenith is immune to environmental hazards and takes no penalties relating to weather or terrain.<br /> <b>War:</b> Battlegroups the Zenith commands possess Might +1 (max 2).</div> <br /> Additionally, she adds (Essence/2, round down) non-charm dice to any action using her Supernal ability.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Solar Exalted - Twilight Caste</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>For five motes, the Twilight projects an aura of pure force, reflexively gaining five Hardness for one turn. At the bonfire/iconic level, this power activates itself automatically at no cost. This effect doesn\u2019t stack with other magic that raises Hardness, but it can be used during Initiative Crash.</i></div> <br /> <b>Protecting Heaven\u2019s Lamp</b><br /> Cost: 5i; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: - (Twilight Caste-only)<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> For the remainder of the scene the cost to trigger The Twilight\u2019s aura of force is now (5 - Essence) motes. In addition to Hardness it also provides 5 bonus Soak whilst this evocation is active; which stacks with natural soak, but not armour. She may activate this when invoking this anima power or whilst she is at bonfire anima.<br /> <br /> <b>Impenetrable Wall of Adamant</b><br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Protecting Heaven's Lamp</i><br /> Whilst it's pre-requisite is active, the Hardness and Soak of the Twilight's anima increase by (Essence).<br /> <br /> <b>Shield of Copper Flame</b><br /> Cost: 8m; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Stackable<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Impenetrable Wall of Adamant</i><br /> The Twilight may extend the Hardness of her anima to (Essence) allies within medium range, who then activate it for the same mote cost as her or gain it automatically whilst she is at Bonfire level, all glowing with hues of her anima. Alternatively she may extend this protection to a Battle Group she commands with a Size of no more than her (Essence) within Medium range.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <i>For 10 motes, one Willpower, the Twilight\u2019s anima flares blue and white and consumes her body over the course of the round. On her next turn, she vanishes into her anima and ceases to exist. If the Exalt moves or suffers knockdown before the action is completed, it fails and the effect is wasted. After using this power, the Twilight will not reappear until the following sunset. When she does, it will be at a place of power within 10 miles of her vanishing point, chosen by the Storyteller. She might appear at a temple, a demesne, a major crossroads, the door of a god\u2019s sanctum, the precise center of a city, etc.</i></div> <br /> <b>Sun\u2019s Well-Trodden Path</b><br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Perilous, (Twilight Caste-only)<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> After vanishing into her anima, the Twilight may reappear at a place of power within (Essence)x10 miles. Furthermore, she may roll her Willpower against a difficulty of 3. Success allows her to choose an eligible place of power within range that she has previously visited.<br /> <br /> <b>Solar Lightning Prana</b><br /> Cost: +1WP; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Sun\u2019s Well-Trodden Path</i><br /> When the Twilight vanishes into her anima, the blue and white flash of her anima arcs outward in all directions to short range, creating an environmental hazard that lasts (Essence) rounds, deals (Essence/2) Lethal/round, with (Essence) difficulty. <br /> <br /> <b>Horizon-Defeating Duplication Technique</b><br /> Cost: 5i; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites:<i> Solar Lightning Prana</i><br /> When the Twilight vanishes, her anima remains; a rippling blue and white and gold simulacrum ready to cover her escape. The duplicate is not truly alive and gives off light as an anima at Burning level. The replica has the Twilight\u2019s memories, intimacies and traits, but is obviously inhuman and lacks her magical equipment. It possesses her Peripheral mote pool, may only use the Twilight\u2019s excellencies and has (Essence) health levels. It cannot use her anima powers or Evocations, but can make Lance attacks. The replica fades at the end of the scene, when it takes any damage to it\u2019s final health level, or it runs out of motes. Once per session.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>For 10 motes, the Twilight may touch an Essence 1-3 elemental or a demon of the first circle, conjoining its Essence to her anima. Roll Intelligence + Occult against the creature\u2019s Resolve. If successful, this creates a pact that changes the spirit into her familiar, allowing her to target it with applicable Survival Charms. In addition, the Twilight can reflexively summon the spirit instantly for three motes, drawing it through the Essence of the world to appear beside her. She may banish the creature again, reflexively, for free, returning it to the tides of Essence that suffuse Creation until needed. The Twilight may have up to (Essence) spirit familiars bound in this fashion at once.</i></div> <br /> <b>Beloved Majordomo</b><br /> Cost: 3i; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous, (Twilight Caste-only)<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> The Twilight values her spirit familiars as more than mere tools or puppets, they are allies, confidants and perhaps even friends. If one of her spirit familiars would be destroyed, she may reflexively recall it into her anima. Whilst dispersed within her anima it heals one level of damage of any type per day, but may not be summoned again until it is fully healed.<br /> <br /> <b>Eternal Warlord Stance</b><br /> Cost: - (1ahl); Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Beloved Majordomo</i><br /> The Twilight may use her anima to bind a Battlegroup comprising all the same type of spirit, in place of a single demon or elemental. This causes her a level of aggravated damage that cannot heal as long as the familiar bond remains; her anima straining to contain the multitude of spirits. A Battlegroup counts as a number of spirits equal to its Size.<br /> <br /> <b>Sovereign Entourage Attitude</b><br /> Cost: - (1ahl, 1WP); Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Celestial Circle Sorcery, Eternal Warlord Stance</i><br /> For 1WP the Twilight may make a demon or elemental of any essence rating into a spirit familiar. This causes her a level of aggravated damage that cannot heal as long as the familiar bond remains, her anima straining to contain the spirit's immense power. Second Circle demons and Essence 4-6 Elementals count as three spirits, Third Circle Demons and Lesser Elemental Dragons count as five spirits.<br /> <br /> <b>Guardian Force Assumption</b><br /> Cost: 8m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only, Perilous<br /> Duration: One Scene or Until Slain<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Horizon-Defeating Duplication Technique, Shield of Copper Flame, Sovereign Entourage Attitude</i><br /> It is the nature of the guard to take an arrow meant for their Mistress. If the Twilight would be hit by a decisive attack she may select any spirit familiar bound to her anima; if it is materialised it will be transported instantly to her location, otherwise it materializes without cost. The Twilight herself vanishes Elsewhere for the duration. The spirit takes the damage of the attack for her, as if it had taken a successful Defend Other action - the attacker may not choose to target the Twilight, who for the moment no longer exists. If it survives, for the rest of the scene it gains a Defining Tie of Murderous Hatred towards the attacker and the Major Principle \u201cI must destroy my master\u2019s enemies\u201d, adding (Twilight\u2019s Essence) to every dice pool in furtherance of those Intimacies. The Twilight returns from Elsewhere where the spirit is slain at the end of that turn; if not killed then the spirit dies at the end of the scene regardless, its duty done.<br /> <br /> <b>Avatar of the Descending Sun</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Guardian Force Assumption</i><br /> The Twilight is the embodiment of the Sun's facet her caste represents, her Anima rising to iconic level and unable to subside or be shed until the end of the scene. Whilst this Evocation is active, she awakens the power from the list below that matches her Supernal ability and (Essence-3) others:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Bureaucracy: </b>The Twilight reveals a completed Project a bureaucracy she leads has undertaken in secret and may benefit accordingly. Once per session.<br /> <b>Craft: </b>The Twilight rolls (Charisma+Craft), difficulty 1 (Basic), 3 (Major) or 6 (Superior), to reflexively manifest a mundane item she could make, changeable once per round. Creations do not grant craft xp and fade at the end of the scene.<br /> <b>Integrity: </b>The Twilight is immune to psyche keyword charms.<br /> <b>Investigation: </b>Unless resisted with magic, the Twilight automatically succeeds on profiling any person she lays her eyes upon who lacks a negative intimacy towards her.<br /> <b>Linguistics: </b>The Twilight understands, speaks, reads and may write all languages as well as a native speaker. <br /> <b>Lore:</b> The Twilight may introduce a single fact that is not internally consistent, but remains a fact until the end of the scene. Once per story.<br /> <b>Medicine:</b> All allies (including herself) within Short range of the Twilight heal one bashing or lethal damage every round.<br /> <b>Occult:</b> All spirits within medium range of the Twilight are made either material and immaterial, whichever she prefers, changeable reflexively once per round.</div> <br /> Additionally, she adds (Essence/2, round down) non-charm dice to any action using her Supernal ability.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Solar Exalted - Night Caste</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>For two motes, the Night can dampen her anima, treating all Peripheral Essence expenditures as if they were Personal for one instant.</i></div> <br /> <b>Efficient Shading Prana</b><br /> Cost: +2m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Mute (Night Caste-only)<br /> Duration: (Essence+1) rounds<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> The Night\u2019s awakened anima allows her greater finesse in manipulating its light. By spending +2 motes when dampening her anima, no peripheral expenditure will raise her anima for (Essence+1) rounds, without the need to pay further motes to do so.<br /> <br /> <b>Vanishing Light</b><br /> Cost: 5i; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Efficient Shading Prana</i><br /> The Night\u2019s anima actively wishes to conceal itself, inverting the flow of essence. When the Night expends 5 peripheral motes (or sorcerous equivalents), she may also spend 5 initiative to reduce her anima by one level (minimum Dim), rather than increasing it. <br /> <br /> <b>Ravenous Darkness Technique</b><br /> Cost: 4i; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Vanishing Light</i><br /> Tracing Five Days Darkness\u2019 name in the air, the Night inflicts her own boon upon others. Her target\u2019s anima is immediately reduced to Dim level, the Night receives 3 motes for each level it was reduced by. <br /> <br /> This charm cannot affect a target under the effect of an <i>Avatar of the \u2026 Sun/Dragon/Moon</i> Evocation.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <i>For three motes, the Night can ignore up to (higher of 3 or Essence) penalties to a Stealth attempt for one instant. These motes are always considered Personal, regardless of the pool they\u2019re spent from.</i></div> <br /> <b>Sharing Shadows Style</b><br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: - (Night Caste-only)<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> When the Night uses her anima to ignore less stealth penalties than her maximum, she may transfer the excess to an ally in Medium range, reducing penalties on their next stealth roll in the same round.<br /> <br /> <b>Distracted Guards Are Blind</b><br /> Cost: 5i; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: One round<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Sharing Shadows Style</i><br /> When an ally makes a Stealth check that the Night is aware of, she may activate this Evocation to inflict an (Essence) penalty on their Stealth check. This allows her to double the number of Stealth penalties she can ignore with her anima power on her next check before the end of the next round.<br /> <br /> <b>Secret Identity Affect</b><br /> Cost: +2m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Distracted Guards Are Blind</i><br /> The Night is able to conceal her spirit as well as her body. Instead of ignoring stealth penalties with her anima power, she may instead deceive a single instance of magical identification; such as tricking a God using Measure the Wind into thinking she is a mortal.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <i>When the Night\u2019s anima is at the bonfire/iconic level, it wraps around and suffuses her form, hiding her figure and masking her visage in flame. She is merely a fearsome silhouette shrouded in all the hues of evening. It becomes impossible to discern her identity. This is considered a perfect effect, and cannot be pierced by Eye of the Unconquered Sun (see p. 273) or other all-seeing magic.</i></div> <br /> <b>Sun In Your Eyes</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Dual, Perilous, (Night Caste-only)<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> Whilst at bonfire/iconic anima the Night angles the flaring light at her attackers, reducing their Parry/Dodge against her attacks by (Essence/2).<br /> <br /> <b>False Reflection Stance</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: Until anima reduces below bonfire/iconic<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Sun In Your Eyes</i><br /> Whilst her identity is concealed by her bonfire anima, the Night bends the light it sheds around her, creating a false image. She rolls (Perception+Larceny) vs Guile, anyone who sees her and whose Guile is beaten sees the Night as any person she chooses, to whom she has a Tie of any intensity. Identity-discerning magic suffers a -3 penalty if the Tie is Defining.<br /> <br /> <b>Hiding Fire In Flames </b><br /> Cost: 5i; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>False Reflection Stance</i><br /> Rolling (Dex+Stealth), the Night must successfully enter concealment whilst at Bonfire anima level in order to activate this evocation. If she does then her anima becomes a violet simulacrum that distracts opponents, allowing the night to slink away. <br /> <br /> The duplicate is not truly alive and gives off light as an anima at Burning level. The replica has the Night\u2019s traits, but is obviously inhuman and lacks her magical equipment. It possesses her Peripheral mote pool, may only use the Night\u2019s excellencies and has (Essence) health levels. It cannot use her anima powers or Evocations, but can make Lance attacks. The replica fades when it takes any damage to its final health level, it runs out of motes, or the Night leaves concealment. Once per session.<br /> <br /> <b>Left and Right Harmony Technique</b><br /> Cost: 1lhl, 1WP; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Hiding Fire In Flames, Ravenous Darkness Technique, Secret Identity Affect</i><br /> Physically drawing blood, the Night\u2019s mote pools also bleed into one another. For the rest of the scene, the Night and (Essence) allies are treated as having only Personal motes. Their Personal and Peripheral pools are combined and never cause their anima to rise. Likewise, Shaping (or Distort/Counterspell) actions that garner 5+ successes do not cause her anima to rise. <br /> <br /> <b>Avatar of the Hidden Sun</b><br /> Cost: 10m (+2m), 1WP; Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Psyche<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Left and Right Harmony Technique</i><br /> The Night is the embodiment of the Sun's facet her caste represents, her Anima rising to iconic level and unable to subside or be shed until the end of the scene, unless she has Stealth as a Supernal or Caste ability and pays +2 motes to instead reduce it to Dim for the scene. Whilst this Evocation is active, she awakens the power from the list below that matches her Supernal ability and (Essence-3) others:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Athletics: </b>The Night adds her (Essence) to her Strength when determining what Feats of Strength and Destruction she can undertake.<br /> <b>Awareness: </b>The Night may substitute any sense for another without penalty. She can smell textures and see songs.<br /> <b>Dodge:</b> The Night may apply her Dodge defence against an undodgeable attack for 1WP.<br /> <b>Investigation: </b>Unless resisted with magic, the Night automatically succeeds on profiling any person she lays her eyes upon who lacks a negative intimacy towards her.<br /> <b>Larceny:</b> The Night\u2019s actions taken whilst using this power can never be proven unlawful or to have broken an edict, taboo or similar restriction.<br /> <b>Ride: </b>The Night\u2019s mount adds (her Essence) to its speed bonus whilst she rides it.<br /> <b>Stealth:</b> If the Night negates her anima rising, when the scene ends nobody can remember the Night\u2019s actions whilst using this power unless they have a Major or Defining positive Tie towards her.<br /> <b>Socialise:</b> Minor negative Ties towards the Night are suppressed for the scene. They cannot be used in social influence.</div> <br /> Additionally, she adds (Essence/2, round down) non-charm dice to any action using her Supernal ability.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Solar Exalted - Eclipse Caste</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>For 10 motes, one Willpower, the Eclipse sanctifies an oath she has witnessed. The Exalt touches the oathgivers (or their words, as they pass through the air), her caste mark flashing imperceptibly. If she wishes, her anima briefly flares, swirling with the words and runes by which Heaven has given her the right to arbitrate such matters.<br /> <br /> Oath-givers who break pacts sanctified by the Eclipse (including the Exalt herself) are subject to a terrible curse. The details of the curse are devised by the Storyteller, ideally reflecting the oath broken. A woman who breaks a hospitality oath might find herself incapable of rest beneath any roof for a year and a day, while a man who murdered the one he swore to protect may find his defenses utterly failing him when he must next fight for his life.</i></div> <br /> <b>Revelation Upon Solar Winds</b><br /> Cost: (1m); Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: - , (Eclipse Caste-only)<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> The Eclipse instantly knows when someone breaks an oath she has sanctified. For 1m she may share this fact across any distance with all other parties to the oath. They don\u2019t necessarily know the Eclipse did this, but they know deep in their soul that they have been betrayed.<br /> <br /> <b>Careless Words Weigh Heavy</b><br /> Cost: -; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Revelation Upon Solar Winds</i><br /> Heaven keeps track of its debtors. The Eclipse is made aware when someone bound by an oath that she has sanctified seeks to voluntarily enter a new agreement with another party. At that time she may choose to sanctify that additional oath, quietly burdening them with an ever growing responsibility to live up to their word.<br /> <br /> <b>Justice-Defining Premonition</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Careless Words Weigh Heavy</i><br /> Entering a deep trance, the Eclipse seeks an audience with the arbiters of Heaven. After roughly one hour she will be granted this audience; at this point she may attempt to recommend an appropriate punishment for either or both parties to an oath she has previously sanctified. These beings have Resolve 8, a charm equivalent to Excellent Solar Integrity and the following intimacies: <i>&quot;We are charged to determine the fate of oath-breakers&quot; (Defining), &quot;Woe betide those who offend us&quot; (Major), &quot;Justice above all&quot; (Major)</i>. If she succeeds, her plan will be followed as closely as possible, subject to storyteller adjudication. If she fails to convince the arbiters they cast her out; she gains a point of Limit for her hubris and may not use this Evocation again in this story.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <i>The Eclipse has diplomatic immunity when treating with the enemies of Creation. So long as the Eclipse approaches them on legitimate business of some kind, shades, spirits, the demon princes of Hell, and the Fair Folk may not attack the Eclipse or her companions without just cause, and such creatures must observe the local rules of hospitality. Such beings may still attempt to provoke members of the Solar\u2019s embassy into breaking the peace, thus voiding this effect\u2019s protection.</i></div> <br /> <b>Consummate Ambassador Approach</b><br /> Cost:1m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: - (Eclipse Caste-only)<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> When exercising diplomatic immunity, the Eclipse will not leave until her business is concluded. Her fatigue and wound penalties are treated as zero (but she does not actually recover from such penalties), allowing her to go without food, rest or medical treatment for as long as her negotiations last. <br /> <br /> <b>Pleasant Embassy Meditation</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Consummate Ambassador Approach</i><br /> The Eclipse is an expert at setting Creation\u2019s enemies at ease. Whilst exercising diplomatic immunity, this Evocation allows the Eclipse to automatically discern one of her opposite number\u2019s Defining intimacies without needing to succeed on a Read Intentions roll. Once per target. This is a perfect effect, that opposition magic cannot detect.<br /> <br /> <b>Aggressive Negotiations Technique</b><br /> Cost: 8i, 1a; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: (Essence rounds)<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Pleasant Embassy Meditation</i><br /> Directing the Mudra of Parlay at an opponent after Join Battle is rolled, the Eclipse throws up her anima as a flag of truce. Roll (Manipulation+Socialise) against the higher of the target\u2019s Resolve or Parry, if successful the rules of diplomatic immunity are enforced regardless of who or what they are; the being may not strike and neither may the Eclipse\u2019s allies. Other opponents are not subject to the rules unless they are direct subordinates of the bound target. <br /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <i>The Eclipse represents all the subtle movements of Essence under Heaven, the strange and self-referencing powers that stir when night merges with day. Eclipses can learn the Charms of spirits, Fair Folk and similar supernatural beings which have the Eclipse keyword for eight experience points each.|</i></div> <br /> <b>Network of Peers Protocol</b><br /> Cost: -; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: - , (Eclipse Caste-only)<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> The Eclipse is an expert in the subtleties of essence. She may now learn Eclipse-keyword charms known by others besides their originators. This includes other Eclipse castes, as well as those under the effects of Gloaming Eye Understanding or Transference of Power Prana.<br /> <br /> <b>Transference of Power Prana</b><br /> Cost: 1WP; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Stackable<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Pre-requisites:<i> Network of Peers Protocol </i><br /> The Eclipse picks an Eclipse-keyword charms she has learned and offers it as a gift to a being with a mote pool. If they accept, they commit three motes to the Eclipse, which are added to her peripheral mote pool, increasing it by three for the duration of this Evocation. They may now use the charm as they wish, but the Eclipse loses access to it for the duration. Only the receiving party may end the commitment to return the charm to the Eclipse. She may give away up to (Essence/2) charms at once.<br /> <br /> <b>Twin-Faced Solar Solution</b><br /> Cost: 7m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: - <br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Transference of Power Prana</i><br /> Meditating on the phases of the sun\u2019s journey across the sky, the Eclipse is able to tap into the blessings of the other Solar Castes. To use this Evocation, she and a willing Solar each display their caste marks and the Eclipse temporarily replaces one of her anima powers with the corresponding power of the other Solar\u2019s caste. Whilst this charm remains committed the other Solar cannot use this power, but whenever they regain motes or Willpower they regain an additional point of each. Neither loses any Lance Evocations, but those relating to the lost anima powers cease to function, this one excluded. The Eclipse cannot access any Eclipse-keyword charms for the duration.<br /> <br /> <b>The Voice of Calibration</b><br /> Cost: 15m; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Up to 5 days<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Aggressive Negotiations Technique, Justice-Defining Premonition, Twin-Faced Solar Solution</i><br /> During Calibration, the borders of Creation and the other realms are thin and passage is made possible. With this Evocation the Eclipse may address any being not native to Creation and request passage to their home realm. She rolls (Charisma+Socialise) vs Resolve, and if successful, she, up to (Essence) others and the being are immediately transported to that realm. Whilst there, for up to five days she is considered to be on legitimate business for the purposes of diplomatic immunity. After that time her blanket protection fades, but she may still approach the enemies of Creation as normal. At any time before the five days end, she, her allies and opponent may return to where they left from. <br /> <br /> <b>Avatar of the Crowned Sun</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Pilot<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>The Voice of Calibration</i><br /> The Eclipse is the embodiment of the Sun's facet her caste represents, her Anima rising to iconic level and unable to subside or be shed until the end of the scene. Whilst this Evocation is active, she awakens the power from the list below that matches her Supernal ability and (Essence-3) others:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Bureaucracy: </b>The Eclipse reveals a Project a bureaucracy she leads has completed and may benefit accordingly. Once per session.<br /> <b>Larceny:</b> The Eclipse\u2019s actions taken whilst using this power can never be proven unlawful or to have broken an edict, taboo or similar restriction.<br /> <b>Linguistics: </b>The Eclipse understands, speaks, reads and may write all languages as well as a native speaker. <br /> <b>Occult: </b>All spirits within medium range of the Eclipse are made either material and immaterial, whichever she prefers, changeable reflexively once per round.<br /> <b>Presence: </b> Any opponent within Long range of the Eclipse must move a range band towards her every round unless they roll (Willpower), difficulty (Eclipse's Essence/2).<br /> <b>Ride: </b>The Eclipse\u2019s mount adds (her Essence) to it\u2019s speed bonus while she rides it.<br /> <b>Sail:</b> Any vessel captained by the Eclipse reduces the Momentum cost of Stratagems by her (Essence, minimum 1).<br /> <b>Socialise:</b> Minor negative Ties towards the Eclipse are suppressed for the scene. They cannot be used in social influence.</div> <br /> Additionally, she adds (Essence/2, round down) non-charm dice to any action using her Supernal ability.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Solar Exalted - Special</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Should a Solar Exalt of each caste activate their respective <i>Avatar of the \u2026 Sun</i> Evocation in the same scene, then be combined by the spell \u2018Unity of the Closed Fist\u2019, the composite being automatically unlocks the following Evocation at no XP cost.<br /> <br /> <b>The Second Sun</b><br /> Cost: 100m, 10WP; Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant (until Unity of the Closed Fist ends)<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Avatar of the Ascending Sun, Avatar of the Crowned Sun, Avatar of the Descending Sun, Avatar of the Hidden Sun, Avatar of the Resplendent Sun, Solar Circle Sorcery</i><br /> So perfect is this unification of the Sun\u2019s facets, that Fate itself cannot tell the Sorcerer apart from the true Unconquered Sun. The composite being shares his every authority and privilege in Heaven; they may look into the flames of Exigence and grant requests for its power from lesser divinities, or speak to a Zenith caste at the moment of their Second Breath. Further, they are treated as possessing Cult 6 and Influence (Yu Shan) 6, claiming worship and Ambrosia meant for Sol Invictus. The God of Gods within the Jade Pleasure Dome certainly notices this holy doppelganger, but what he does is up to the Storyteller.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T16:10:11-08:00","id":1472280,"title":"","content":"Duplicate post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T16:14:10-08:00","id":1472281,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b>Dragonblood Evocations</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Air Aspect </b>- <i>The Dragonblood\u2019s Lance is treated as a blue jade weapon for any relevant purposes</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>For five motes, the Air Aspect can use her reflexive move action to leap an entire range band vertically or horizontally without needing to roll, and suffers no falling damage for the rest of the round. At bonfire, this power is free.</i></div> <br /> <b>Air Cannon Technique</b><br /> Cost: 6m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Withering-only, (Air Aspect-only)<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> Upon making a successful withering attack, the Air Aspect may forgo the initiative lost by her target to launch them up to (Essence/2) range bands vertically or horizontally. She still gains 1i for landing a successful attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Flying Hurricane Manoeuvre </b><br /> Cost: 4i; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive <br /> Keywords: -, <br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites:<i> Air Cannon Technique</i><br /> Once per session, the Air Aspect may unleash a blast of air and move vertically or horizontally up to (Essence) range bands. She takes no falling damage for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>For three motes, the Air Aspect may deflect projectiles with a gust of wind, imposing a \u22121 environmental penalty on all ranged attacks against her until her next turn.</i></div> <br /> <b>Razor Wind Stance</b><br /> Cost: 4m, 3i; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords:- , (Air Aspect-only)<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> The Air Aspect surrounds herself in whirlwinds. As well as providing an (Essence/2) penalty on all ranged attacks against her, she is considered to be using anima flux regardless of her anima level.<br /> <br /> <b>Slipstream Slice Technique</b><br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Permanent <br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Razor Wind Stance</i><br /> The Air Aspect manipulates the air to clear a path for her blades. Whilst under the effect of Razor Wind Stance she is treated as having an all-encompassing specialty for Thrown attacks.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>Once per day, when the Air Aspect takes a nonextended social or mental action to uphold a Principle, she adds (Intimacy) non-Charm bonus dice on the roll.</i></div> <br /> <b>Unending Current Approach</b><br /> Cost: 4m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: - Supplemental<br /> Keywords: -, (Air Aspect-only)<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> The Air Aspect receives (Intimacy) non-charm dice on any further actions to uphold the Principle she has already protected with her anima that day.<br /> <br /> <b>Heart of Ice Method</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: One Session<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Unending Current Approach</i><br /> The Air Aspect freezes her emotions. Once per session she may select a Major or Defining intimacy to lock in ice; she may act against that intimacy without eroding it or being afflicted by the Great Curse, but cannot use it in social influence either.<br /> <br /> <b>Inexorable Glacier Mudra</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only, Mute<br /> Duration: Essence Days<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Flying Hurricane Manoeuvre, Heart of Ice Method, Slipstream Slice Technique</i><br /> Ice creeps into the soul of the Air Aspect\u2019s enemies. When she lands a ranged decisive attack, she may forgo damage, and instead freeze one of their intimacies - Minor (up to 3 health levels), Major (up to 6 hls) or Defining (7+ hls). The Intimacy is unavailable to the target for the longer of (Essence) days or the remainder of the story, their personality adjusting to match.<br /> <br /> <b>Avatar of the Azure Dragon</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Inexorable Glacier Mudra</i><br /> The Dragonblood becomes the embodiment of her elemental aspect, her Anima rising to iconic level and unable to subside or be shed until the end of the scene, unless she pays +2 motes to instead reduce it to Dim for the scene. Whilst this Evocation is active, she receives (Essence/2) of the following five gifts:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Linguistics:</b> The Air Aspect understands, speaks, reads and may write all languages as well as a native speaker. <br /> <b>Lore: </b>The Air Aspect may introduce a single fact that is not internally consistent, but remains a fact until the end of the scene. Once per story.<br /> <b>Occult:</b> All spirits within medium range of the Air Aspect are made either material and immaterial, whichever she prefers, changeable reflexively once per round<br /> <b>Stealth: </b>If the Air Aspect negates her anima rising, when the scene ends nobody can remember the Air Aspect\u2019s actions whilst using this power unless they have a Major or Defining Tie towards her.<br /> <b>Thrown:</b> The Air Aspect may make thrown attacks at extreme range (up to (Essence) range bands). She must still aim to do so beyond Short range.</div> <br /> Additionally, the blessing of Mela causes each of her Sworn Kin / Hearthmates active alongside her to gain two initiative for successfully landing a withering attack instead of one for the duration of this evocation.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Earth Aspect</b> - <i>The Dragonblood\u2019s Lance is treated as a white jade weapon for any relevant purposes</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>For five motes, the Earth Aspect adds (higher of Essence or 3) natural soak and +1 Hardness until her next turn, as well as gaining +1 Defense against smash attacks and grapple gambits as a non-Charm bonus. At bonfire, this power is free.</i></div> <br /> <b>Stone Armour Approach</b><br /> Cost: 2m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Dual, (Earth Aspect-only)<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> As long as the Earth Aspect is in contact with natural earth or stone, she doubles the bonuses to soak, hardness and defence that her anima provides. She does this by encasing herself in that material, which requires a reflexive difficulty 1 Feat of Destruction as a free action to break out of before she next takes an action.<br /> <br /> <b>Sand Through Fingers Prana</b><br /> Cost: 1i, 1WP; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Stone Armour Approach</i><br /> While under the effect of this Evocation, the Earth Aspect increases the difficulty of any Grapple gambit against her by (Essence) unless her opponent has a specialty of manipulating earth either for Brawl or Craft. At bonfire this increases by a further +1<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>For three motes, the Earth Aspect ignores one point of penalty from wounds, poison, or crippling for a single tick.</i></div> <br /> <b>Granite in the Blood Stance</b><br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: (Earth Aspect-only)<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> The Earth Aspect\u2019s anima now protects her from penalties for (Essence rounds) rather than a single tick.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood From a Stone Technique</b><br /> Cost: 7i; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites:<i> Granite in the Blood Stance</i><br /> The Earth Aspect ignores the first (Essence) levels of initiative damage suffered, or the (Essence/2) bashing levels of damage from an attack.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>The Dragon-Blood may spend two Initiative when she rolls anima flux to either knock all damaged foes prone or knock them one range band away from her.</i></div> <br /> <b>Rockslide Approach</b><br /> Cost: 5i; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: -, (Earth Aspect-only)<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> Against a crashed opponent, the Earth Aspect may use her anima flux to roll (Essence+Willpower) to initiate a gambit. If successful, the gambit takes effect as if she had made a decisive roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Seismic Toss Mudra</b><br /> Cost: 2i, 1WP; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: - <br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites:<i> Rockslide Approach</i><br /> Unleashing her wrath, the Earth Aspect can use her anima to instead knock all enemies at short range from her up to (Essence) range bands back (max Long).<br /> <br /> <b>Unstoppable Golem Technique</b><br /> Cost: 6i, 1WP; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Blood From a Stone Technique, Sand Through Fingers Prana, Seismic Toss Mudra</i><br /> The Earth Aspect invokes the supreme power of the Pole of Earth and cloaks herself in its divine Jade rubble. She gains (6+Essence) natural soak and hardness. Her earthen limbs deal lethal damage with unarmed attacks. For the duration of this evocation her fatigue and wound penalties are treated as zero (but she does not actually recover from such penalties), and she is immune to environmental hazards based on the five elements. She may roll (Intelligence+Craft) against Difficulty 6 at the end of the scene to condense the rubble into one eighth of a Talent\u2019s worth of Jade currency.<br /> <br /> <b>Avatar of the Ivory Dragon</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Unstoppable Golem Technique</i><br /> The Dragonblood becomes the embodiment of her elemental aspect, her Anima rising to iconic level and unable to subside or be shed until the end of the scene. Whilst this Evocation is active, she receives (Essence/2) of the following five gifts:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Awareness: </b>The Earth Aspect may substitute any sense for another without penalty. She can hear scents and touch flavours.<br /> <b>Craft: </b>The Earth Aspect rolls (Charisma+Craft), difficulty 1 (Basic), 3 (Major) or 6 (Superior), to reflexively manifest a mundane item she could make from nearby earth, changeable once per round. Creations do not grant craft xp and fade at the end of the scene.<br /> <b>Integrity: </b>The Earth Aspect is immune to psyche keyword charms.<br /> <b>Resistance: </b>The Earth Aspect converts half of Aggravated damage to Lethal, and all other Lethal damage to Bashing. Damage still rolls over.<br /> <b>War: </b>Battlegroups the Earth Aspect commands possess Might +1 (max 2).</div> <br /> Additionally, the blessing of Pasiap allows each of her Sworn Kin / Hearthmates active alongside her to treat their base initiative as one higher for the duration of this evocation.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Fire Aspect</b> - <i>The Dragonblood\u2019s Lance is treated as a red jade weapon for any relevant purposes</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>For five motes, the Fire Aspect becomes completely immune to mundane environmental hazards based on fire or heat for a scene. She adds (Essence) natural soak and gains Hardness 2 against fire-based attacks like firewands. She gains these benefits for free while at bonfire.</i></div> <br /> <b>Fire Deterrence Prana</b><br /> Cost: 2i; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental or Reflexive<br /> Keywords: - , (Fire Aspect-only)<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> The Fire Aspect may extend her immunity to mundane flame to (Essence) allies within:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Short range if her anima is at Dim or Glowing level;<br /> Medium range if it is at Burning level; or</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Long range if it is at Bonfire level.</div> <br /> <b>Inhaling Embers Practise</b><br /> Cost: 3m, 1a; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Fire Deterrence Prana</i><br /> When the Fire Aspect successfully defends against a withering attack from a fire-based weapon or magical attack, she gains (Essence) bonus initiative. If she defends against a decisive attack, she heals (Essence/2) bashing or lethal health levels instead.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>Once per day, when the Fire Aspect takes a nonextended action to uphold an emotion-based Intimacy, she adds (Intimacy) non-Charm bonus dice to the roll.</i></div> <br /> <b>Undying Flame Approach</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: - Supplemental<br /> Keywords: -, (Fire Aspect-only)<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> The Fire Aspect receives (Intimacy) non-charm dice on any further actions to uphold the Intimacy she has already protected with her anima that day.<br /> <br /> <b>Burning Heart Method</b><br /> Cost: 4m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: One Session<br /> Pre-requisites:<i> Undying Flame Approach</i><br /> The Fire Aspect ignites her emotions. Once per session she may select a Major or Defining intimacy to flare; anyone with less Willpower than her treats it as their own intimacy at one level lower for the rest of the session.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>A Fire Aspect\u2019s anima flux deals (higher of Essence or 3) damage to characters without Hardness instead of one die.</i></div> <br /> <b>Unstoppable Balefire Spirit</b><br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: -, (Fire Aspect-only)<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> The Fire Aspect\u2019s anima intensifies into a nightmarish conflagration. Her anima flux now deals damage to those with Hardness less than her (Essence) instead of 1.<br /> <br /> <b>Wildfire Spreads Eternal</b><br /> Cost: 7i; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Until Anima drops below bonfire<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Unstoppable Balefire Preparation</i><br /> The Fire Aspect\u2019s anima flux becomes an environmental hazard, affecting everywhere she walks. Wherever she walks remains aflame for 2 rounds. Anyone stepping in her wake must roll (Dexterity+Athletics) difficulty (Essence) or suffer (Essence) Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Scorched Earth Emanation</b><br /> Cost: 10i, 1/2/3a; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only, Psyche<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Burning Heart Method, Inhaling Embers Practise, Wildfire Spreads Eternal</i><br /> The Fire Aspect gathers her anima and unleashes it as a column of flame out to short range. This decisive attack is unblockable but can be dodged. Anyone struck takes no damage, but instead a randomly chosen Principle catches fire depending on the levels of anima spent; Minor (1a), Major (2a) or Defining (3a). For the rest of the scene any action not directly in support of this Principle causes excruciating pain, resulting in the sufferer respiring (Essence/2) less motes at the end of a round. At the end of the scene, all those affected must pay (Essence) Willpower or their Principle degrades one level, minor Principles disintegrating like ash.<br /> <br /> <b>Avatar of the Crimson Dragon</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Scorched Earth Emanation</i><br /> The Dragonblood becomes the embodiment of her elemental aspect, her Anima rising to iconic level and unable to subside or be shed until the end of the scene. Whilst this Evocation is active, she receives (Essence/2) of the following five gifts:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Athletics:</b> The Fire Aspect adds her (Essence) to her Strength when determining what Feats of Strength and Destruction she can undertake.<br /> <b>Dodge:</b> The Fire Aspect may apply her Dodge defence against an undodgeable attack for 1WP.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Melee: </b>The Fire Aspect may apply her Parry defence against an unblockable attack for 1WP.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Presence:</b> Any opponent within Long range of the Fire Aspect must move a range band towards her every round unless they roll (Willpower+Resolve), difficulty (Fire Aspect\u2019s Essence).<br /> <b>Socialise:</b> Minor negative Ties towards the Fire Aspect are suppressed for the scene. They cannot be used in social influence.<br /> </div> <br /> Additionally, the blessing of Hesiesh allows each of her Sworn Kin / Hearthmates active alongside her to reduce their onslaught penalty by one for the duration of this evocation (minimum 0).<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Water Aspect</b> - <i>The Dragonblood\u2019s Lance is treated as a black jade weapon for any relevant purposes</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>For five motes, the Water Aspect may use her move action to cross the surface of water as though it were solid land, and ignores the \u22123 penalty for rushing or disengaging across difficult terrain. She gains these benefits for free while at bonfire.</i></div> <br /> <b>Water Striding Speed</b><br /> Cost: 5i; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous, (Water Aspect-only)<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> Whilst standing on water the Water Aspect\u2019s movement speed doubles, allowing her to reflexively move two range bands each turn instead of one. She may activate this when invoking this anima power or whilst she is at bonfire anima.<br /> <br /> <b>Shield From the Sea</b><br /> Cost: 3i; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: One Tick<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Water Striding Speed</i><br /> Whilst on or within close range of a water source, the Water Aspect may reflexively take cover, causing a wall of water to rise between her and her enemy\u2019s weapon. This counts as full cover, or partial cover if the only water available is less than a flowing river or lake. Less than a barrel of water makes this evocation unusable.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>For three motes, the Water Aspect adds a nonCharm success on a roll to disengage, withdraw, or resist being grappled.</i></div> <br /> <b>Flowing River Style</b><br /> Cost: +1m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Uniform, (Water Aspect-only)<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> For one additional mote, when using her anima power the Water Aspect may add (Essence) dice to a roll instead of a single automatic success.<br /> <br /> <b>Endless Shoreline Style</b><br /> Cost: +2m; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites:<i> Flowing River Style</i><br /> The Water Aspect may use her anima to add one automatic non-charm success to any action relating to freeing herself from restraints or confinement. This includes freeing herself from a grapple, but not savage, drag or throw actions.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>Water Aspects may breathe water as though it were air, and suffer no penalties for being submerged in water.</i></div> <br /> <b>Shared Breath Prana</b><br /> Cost: 2m+; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental or Reflexive<br /> Keywords: - , (Water Aspect-only)<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>None</i><br /> For 2m each the Water Aspect may extend her ability to breathe underwater to (Essence) allies within:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Short range if her anima is at Dim or Glowing level;<br /> Medium range if it is at Burning level; or</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Long range if it is at Bonfire level.</div> <br /> <b>Mermaid Kick Technique</b><br /> Cost: 5i, (1m+); Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites:<i> Shared Breath Prana</i><br /> The Water Aspect gains a +3 Speed bonus, or 3 automatic charm successes on any Movement-based Athletics rolls whilst underwater. For one mote each, she may share this boon with anyone under the effect of her Shared Breath Prana.<br /> <br /> <b>Living Ship Manifestation</b><br /> Cost: 7m, 3a, 1WP; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Pilot<br /> Duration: One Scene <br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Endless Shoreline Style, Mermaid Kick Technique, Shield From the Sea</i><br /> The Water Aspect casts her anima into a nearby body of water (nothing less than the sea, a large lake or an especially huge waterfall will suffice) unleashing a maelstrom of water at her command. In combat she is treated as having the Legendary Size merit; her actions replicated by a watery goliath which surrounds her. Alternatively in naval combat, the Water Aspect is treated as a ship (which she is captaining), she may use her dice pools to gain Momentum and execute Stratagems. She has Hull equal to her health levels, (Essence) Speed and (Essence/2) Maneuverability. <br /> <br /> <b>Avatar of the Sable Dragon</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Pilot<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <i>Living Ship Manifestation</i><br /> The Dragonblood becomes the embodiment of her elemental aspect, her Anima rising to iconic level and unable to subside or be shed until the end of the scene. Whilst this Evocation is active, she receives (Essence/2) of the following five gifts:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Brawl: </b>The Water Aspect\u2019s unarmed attacks gain the balanced, chopping, lethal, piercing, smashing and two-handed tags. She may parry lethal damage without other magic. </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Bureaucracy: </b>The Water Aspect reveals a Project a bureaucracy she leads has completed and may benefit accordingly. Once per session.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Investigation: </b>Unless resisted with magic, the Water Aspect automatically succeeds on profiling any person she lays her eyes upon who lacks a negative intimacy towards her.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Larceny: </b>The Water Aspect\u2019s actions taken whilst using this power can never be proven unlawful or to have broken an edict, taboo or similar restriction. Members of her Hearth are immune to this power.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Sail:</b> Any vessel captained by the Water Aspect reduces the Momentum cost of Stratagems by (Essence).</div> <br /> Additionally, the blessing of Daana\u2019D causes each of her Sworn Kin / Hearthmates active alongside her to regenerate two extra motes per round for the duration of this evocation.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Wood Aspect</b> - <i>The Dragonblood\u2019s Lance is treated as a green jade weapon for any relevant purposes</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>For five motes, the Wood Aspect becomes immune to mundane plant-based poisons, and doubles 9s on rolls to resist other poisons and diseases for the scene. She gains these benefits for free while at bonfire.</i></div> <br /> <b>Woodsman\u2019s Resolve Aura</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental or Reflexive<br /> Keywords: -, (Wood Aspect-only)<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: None<br /> For 3m each the Wood Aspect may extend her immunity to poisons to (Essence) allies within:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Short range if her anima is at Dim or Glowing level;<br /> Medium range if it is at Burning level; or</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Long range if it is at Bonfire level.</div> <br /> <b>Venomous Chimera Method</b><br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: One Story<br /> Pre-requisites: Woodsman\u2019s Resolve Aura<br /> When the Wood Aspect is exposed to a mundane poison she may imprint its essence pattern into her anima. She must voluntarily suffer the effects of the poison and survive without medical treatment. If she does so, her anima now expresses the traits of that poison for the rest of the story.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>For three motes, the Wood Aspect becomes flexible as a sapling in the wind, ignoring one point of penalty to Evasion or (Essence) points of penalty on a movement action for an instant.</i></div> <br /> <b>Evergreen Stance</b><br /> Cost: +6i; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: (Wood Aspect-only)<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: None<br /> When using her anima to bolster her Evasion in a plant-rich environment, the Wood Aspect may also expend 6i to completely refresh her onslaught penalty to 0.<br /> <br /> <b>Leaves in the Wind Approach</b><br /> Cost: +1WP; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Instant (One Scene)<br /> Pre-requisites: Evergreen Stance<br /> For 1WP when using her anima for a movement action, any penalties she would ignore are instead converted into a bonus on the move action. She gains half that amount as a speed bonus for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>A Wood Aspect\u2019s anima flux is laced with toxic power. A character that takes damage from it is exposed to a poison with Damage 2i/round, Duration (Essence + Stamina) rounds, and a \u22121 penalty</i></div> <br /> <b>Cruel Arrow </b><br /> Cost: 3i; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only, (Wood Aspect-only)<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: None<br /> As long as her anima is at least at Glowing level, the Wood Aspect may add her anima\u2019s poison to any ranged attack she makes.<br /> <br /> <b>Slinking Vines Motion</b><br /> Cost: 2m; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: One Scene or until discharged<br /> Pre-requisites: Cruel Arrow<br /> Whilst her anima is at Dim level, the Wood Aspect can draw out a dose of it\u2019s poison onto her skin. This version has the same stats but is Touch vector.<br /> <br /> <b>Wicked Thorns Rebuke</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Counter-attack, Perilous, Uniform, Withering-only<br /> Duration: Until discharged<br /> Pre-requisites: Leaves in the Wind Approach, Slinking Vines Motion, Venomous Chimera Method<br /> When the Wood Aspect evades an attack successfully she may counterattack in kind, covering her enemy in venomous moss. This is a withering attack using either a ranged weapon in hand or her Lance, which inflicts her anima\u2019s poison on contact. She may continue to counteract by paying motes but not WP each time until she fails to evade an attack, fails to land a counterattack or enters initiative crash.<br /> <br /> <b>Avatar of the Emerald Dragon</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1WP; Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: <br /> The Dragonblood becomes the embodiment of her elemental aspect, her Anima rising to iconic level and unable to subside or be shed until the end of the scene. Whilst this Evocation is active, she receives (Essence/2) of the following five gifts:<br /> <b>Archery:</b> The Wood Aspect may make archery attacks at extreme range (up to (Essence) range bands). She must still aim to do so.<br /> <b>Medicine:</b> All allies (including herself) within Short range of the Wood Aspect heal one bashing or lethal damage every round.<br /> <b>Performance:</b> Allies within Long range of the Wood Caste are inspired by her perfect elegance, gaining (her Essence/2) additional motes at the end of the round.<br /> <b>Ride:</b> The Wood Aspect\u2019s mount adds her (Essence) to its speed bonus while she rides it.<br /> <b>Survival: </b>The Wood Aspect is immune to environmental hazards and takes no penalties relating to weather or terrain.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the blessing of Sextes Jylis allows each of her Sworn Kin / Hearthmates active alongside her to treat their Wound Penalty as one lower for the duration of this Evocation (minimum 0).<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}